te — grep across all 23 files that reference ReviewSources/RegistryReviewSources confirms every other consumer (publication.ts, coordinator.ts, admission.ts, projection-intervals.ts, packet.ts, controller.ts, cleanup.ts, assessment.ts, task-review-rpc.ts, route-documents.test.ts, route-admission.test.ts, qualification.test.ts, publication-fixture.ts, historical-fixture.ts, derived-unit.test.ts, derived-completion.test.ts, capacity.test.ts) only consumes a RegistryReviewSources instance or the ReviewSources type, never a bare object literal, so none of them need a pathChanges addition. The described pathContinuity replacement (walk only commits from sources.pathChanges filtered by isAncestor, compare existence against each from/ancestor parent, exempt selected origins) preserves the outcome of today's seen-set BFS walk for every edge case the LLD's own table lists, given git's --full-history semantics as described (no simplification, merges matching one parent still listed) match actual git log behavior for a pathspec-restricted history. No HIGH or MED defect found in this chunk's claims against the current code.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md#2.3 (RegistryReviewSources)","message":"The pathChanges call example `callTool(gitPathHistoryTool, { rev: from..to, path, fullHistory: true })` omits `cwd: this.deps.repoPath`, which every other RegistryReviewSources method (object/commit/isAncestor/file/changedRanges) passes explicitly in src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts. Likely just elided for brevity, but worth stating explicitly so a builder does not default to process.cwd() instead of the repo path.","evidenceReferences":["src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts:47 (object: cwd: this.deps.repoPath)","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts:65 (isAncestor: cwd: this.deps.repoPath)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-pa