eview-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md ## 5. Test strategy, integration level, and the ac1 row of the acceptance-mapping table","message":"The integration test subject says it must show 'cost independent of untouched commits' using fixtures N=4 and N=40 untouched commits, but the LLD never states what quantity is measured or how the two runs are compared (e.g. asserting ProjectionBudget.reads/file() call count is equal, or bounded by a constant, for N=4 vs N=40). The ISSUE's whole defect is that cost grows with unrelated commits (c1-c3 in ISSUE-66d4d41d99f805af), so ac1 is the test that must actually demonstrate the fix, not just that the code runs without error for both N values. As specified, a test titled 'lineage reads do not grow with interleaved commits that leave the selected path untouched' could be satisfied by merely not throwing for both fixtures, without asserting the read count stays flat -- a vacuous demonstration of the core fix.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:197 (integration fixtures: 'temporary repo with a selected change followed by N commits and merges that touch only other files (N = 4 and N = 40)')","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:208 (ac1 row: 'lineage reads do not grow with interleaved commits that leave the selected path untouched')","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts:19 (ProjectionBudget.read() is the countable quantity that should be asserted stable across N)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/ISSUE.md:9 (reproduction: 'read src/workflow/gates.ts 119 times ... before the 64 MiB cap stopped it' -- the defect is literally a read-count-vs-unrelated-commits relationship, which the test must measure)"]},{"id":"ac5-smoke-row-format-inconsistent","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md ## 5. Test strategy, acceptance-mapping table, ac5 row","message":"ac1-ac4 name a concrete `<file>: <test title>` pair as the proving test, but ac5 names only prose ('smoke: the eedc4519199b24b4/s1 correction packet at pin 92491bba9 prepares without projection_limit (reported)') with no file/test-title and only a parenthetical '(reported)' marker. This is workable (the smoke level is explicitly a manual/reported case per the test-strategy section), but the inconsistent row format in the same table makes the mapping harder to machine-trace during build/validate, where insrc_build_step expects either a file+title mapping or an explicit reported{result,evidence} for a smoke/live test it cannot run itself.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:200 (smoke test level description)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:212 (ac5 row)"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/projection.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider making the integration test for ac1 assert the ProjectionBudget read counter (or an equivalent exposed count) 