","/body/alternativesConsidered/2"],"concerns":["Verify the migration's state-before description matches projection.ts's actual current line ranges/behavior (pathContinuity, LIMITS, git_path_history lacking full-history) rather than a stale or imprecise account.","Confirm the 4 migration steps are correctly ordered (tool flag before ReviewSources method before pathContinuity switch before deploy) and each is genuinely independently rollbackable as claimed.","Verify the backward-compat claim that ReviewSources is internal with a single production implementer, so no IPC/plugin exposure is broken by the required-method addition.","Assess whether a1 (chosen) is adequately justified over a2 and a3 given the ISSUE's ac1 requirement (cost must not grow with unrelated commits), and whether the rejection rationale for a2/a3 is factually sound (object-id lookup still scales with commits; graph+diff-tree still one call per edge).","Check that openQuestions being empty is appropriate — i.e., no load-bearing ambiguity (e.g., git full-history edge semantics, hash-length validation for SHA-1 vs SHA-256 repos) was left unresolved that should have been flagged.","Verify costEstimate and pros/cons for each alternative are not internally contradictory with the chosen design's own stated cons (e.g., the 'required method -> ~9 test literals' cost admitted for a1)."],"dependsOn":["contract-data-model"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"summary-scope-and-citations","title":"Summary/scope framing against the originating ISSUE, and citation accuracy/traceability","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7"],"concerns":["Verify the Summary and HLD-context's standalone framing is correct (no HLD applicable) and faithfully restates the ISSUE's fix intent: cost follows changes to reviewed files, not unrelated work, with every existing outcome/limit/id