gnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Status contradicts findings or mandatory verification limits: received changes_requested, expected incomplete; limitations=2, HIGH/MED=1"}],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"migration-and-alternatives","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Status contradicts findings or mandatory verification limits: received passed, expected incomplete; limitations=2, HIGH/MED=0"}],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"summary-scope-and-citations","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Status contradicts findings or mandatory verification limits: received passed, expected incomplete; limitations=2, HIGH/MED=0"}],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"final-consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Status contradicts findings or mandatory verification limits: received changes_requested, expected passed; limitations=0, HIGH/MED=0"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"lld-66d4d41d99f805af-s1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-66d4d41d99f805af-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":1,"LOW":2},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"contract-data-model","status":"passed","summary":"Verified the contract/data-model chunk against the live code: git_path_history (src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts) has no fullHistory option today and the claimed argv-unchanged-when-absent postcondition holds; ReviewSources (sources.ts) has exactly the four methods listed with no existing pathChanges, so the new method is genuinely additive; RegistryReviewSources' object() helper and %H-based PATH_HISTORY_FORMAT support the sha-validation claim; boundedProjectionSources' existing cache-per-key/charge-on-miss pattern for commit/file/changedRanges/isAncestor matches the described treatment for pathChanges; the call-site list in section 3.1 (sources.ts, projection.ts, and the 9 test files) is complete and accurate — grep across all 23 files that reference ReviewSources/RegistryReviewSources confirms every other consumer (publication.ts, coordinator.ts, admission.ts, projection-intervals.ts, packet.ts, controller.ts, cleanup.ts, assessment.ts, task-review-rpc.ts, route-documents.test.ts, route-admission.test.ts, qualification.test.ts, publication-fixture.ts, historical-fixture.ts, derived-unit.test.ts, derived-completion.test.ts, capacity.test.ts) only consumes a RegistryReviewSources instance or the ReviewSources type, never a bare object literal, so none of them need a pathChanges addition. The described pathContinuity replacement (walk only commits from sources.pathChanges filtered by isAncestor, compare existence against each from/ancestor parent, exempt selected origins) preserves the outcome of today's seen-set BFS walk for every edge case the LLD's own table lists, given git's --full-history semantics as described (no simplification, merges matching one parent still listed) match actual git log behavior for a pathspec-restricted history. No HIGH or MED defect found in this chunk's claims against the current code.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md#2.3 (RegistryReviewSources)","message":"The pathChanges call example `callTool(gitPathHistoryTool, { rev: from..to, path, fullHistory: true })` omits `cwd: this.deps.repoPath`, which every other RegistryReviewSources method (object/commit/isAncestor/file/changedRanges) passes explicitly in src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts. Likely just elided for brevity, but worth stating explicitly so a builder does not default to process.cwd() instead of the repo path.","evidenceReferences":["src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts:47 (object: cwd: this.deps.repoPath)","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts:65 (isAncestor: cwd: this.deps.repoPath)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:83"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md","src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/parsers.ts:252-254 (PATH_HISTORY_FORMAT)","src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/helpers.ts:124-129 (assertSafeArg)","src/workflow/git-calls.ts:23,135-137 (pathHistory existing caller)","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection-intervals.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/packet.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/controller.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/cleanup.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/assessment.ts","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/contracts.test.ts:60-70","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/selected-code.test.ts:15-30","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/projection.test.ts:130-148","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/admission-checkpoint.test.ts:38-45","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/history.test.ts:123-132","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/admission.test.ts:72-80","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/ownership.test.ts:54-62","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/projection-intervals.test.ts:70-78","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/coordinator.test.ts:26-35","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/route-documents.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/route-admission.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/qualification.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/publication-fixture.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/historical-fixture.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/derived-unit.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/derived-completion.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/capacity.test.ts:105-117","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/ISSUE.md"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider showing cwd explicitly in the RegistryReviewSources.pathChanges call example in section 2.3 for consistency with the other four methods' documented call shape.","The new test file names (git-path-history-full.test.ts, projection-lineage.test.ts) do not collide with any existing file in the repo, so naming is clear to implement as described."]},{"chunkId":"error-paths-and-tests","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Error-path field semantics (source/scope_conflict/projection_limit) and all five error cases match the existing TaskReviewInputError usage in sources.ts/projection.ts with no repurposing. The edge-case table is consistent with pathContinuity's stated postcondition and with current LIMITS/ProjectionBudget behavior (10000 reads, 100000 fragments, 64 MiB, serial awaits), and the acceptance-mapping (ac1-ac5) traces to named tests that together cover the Story's full fix intent (cost-follows-changes, outcomes unchanged, error-field unchanged, saved-attempt identity unchanged, smoke replay). One MED gap: the integration test strategy names N=4/N=40 fixtures to show \"cost independent of untouched commits\" but never states what is measured or compared, so as written the test could pass without actually demonstrating the root-cause fix. A LOW inconsistency in the acceptance-mapping table's smoke row format is also noted.","findings":[{"id":"cost-independence-unspecified","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md ## 5. Test strategy, integration level, and the ac1 row of the acceptance-mapping table","message":"The integration test subject says it must show 'cost independent of untouched commits' using fixtures N=4 and N=40 untouched commits, but the LLD never states what quantity is measured or how the two runs are compared (e.g. asserting ProjectionBudget.reads/file() call count is equal, or bounded by a constant, for N=4 vs N=40). The ISSUE's whole defect is that cost grows with unrelated commits (c1-c3 in ISSUE-66d4d41d99f805af), so ac1 is the test that must actually demonstrate the fix, not just that the code runs without error for both N values. As specified, a test titled 'lineage reads do not grow with interleaved commits that leave the selected path untouched' could be satisfied by merely not throwing for both fixtures, without asserting the read count stays flat -- a vacuous demonstration of the core fix.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:197 (integration fixtures: 'temporary repo with a selected change followed by N commits and merges that touch only other files (N = 4 and N = 40)')","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:208 (ac1 row: 'lineage reads do not grow with interleaved commits that leave the selected path untouched')","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts:19 (ProjectionBudget.read() is the countable quantity that should be asserted stable across N)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/ISSUE.md:9 (reproduction: 'read src/workflow/gates.ts 119 times ... before the 64 MiB cap stopped it' -- the defect is literally a read-count-vs-unrelated-commits relationship, which the test must measure)"]},{"id":"ac5-smoke-row-format-inconsistent","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md ## 5. Test strategy, acceptance-mapping table, ac5 row","message":"ac1-ac4 name a concrete `<file>: <test title>` pair as the proving test, but ac5 names only prose ('smoke: the eedc4519199b24b4/s1 correction packet at pin 92491bba9 prepares without projection_limit (reported)') with no file/test-title and only a parenthetical '(reported)' marker. This is workable (the smoke level is explicitly a manual/reported case per the test-strategy section), but the inconsistent row format in the same table makes the mapping harder to machine-trace during build/validate, where insrc_build_step expects either a file+title mapping or an explicit reported{result,evidence} for a smoke/live test it cannot run itself.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:200 (smoke test level description)","docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md:212 (ac5 row)"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/code-review-refuses-correction-packet-because-E2026111166d4d41d/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/path-history.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/projection.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider making the integration test for ac1 assert the ProjectionBudget read counter (or an equivalent exposed count) explicitly, and assert it is the same (or near-identical) for the N=4 and N=40 fixtures, to directly falsify a regression to the old per-commit walk.","Consider giving the ac5 row the same `<file>: <test title>` shape used by ac1-ac4 (even if it names a manual runner script or a reported case), or add one sentence in the test-strategy smoke bullet stating explicitly that this is a build-time `reported` test per insrc_build_step's tests contract, so the mapping style is uniform across the table."]},{"chunkId":"migration-and-alternatives","status":"passed","summary":"Verified the migration's state-before account against the actual code (projection.ts pathContinuity lines 51-64, LIMITS at line 9, git_path_history lacking a full-history option), confirmed the 4 migration steps are correctly ordered and each is independently rollbackable, confirmed RegistryReviewSources is the sole production ReviewSources implementer (grep across src/ found no other `implements ReviewSources`), and checked a1's selection over a2/a3 against the ISSUE's cost-must-not-grow-with-unrelated-commits requirement. a2's and a3's rejection rationale is factually sound: a2 keeps the per-commit walk (reads still scale with interleaved commits, just lighter per read), and a3 still issues one diff per edge, so both remain linear in unrelated commits while a1's full-history listing is linear only in commits that touch the selected path — this matches git's documented --full-history semantics (a commit is shown when it is not TREESAME to at least one parent). costEstimate/pros/cons are internally consistent, including a1's own admitted cost of ~9 test-literal rebindings. openQuestions being empty is appropriate: the git full-history edge semantics and SHA-1/SHA-256 hash-length validation that could have been left ambiguous are both addressed explicitly in the co